[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hazelgrove/hazel/pulls/1139","id":1601736557,"node_id":"PR_kwDOBMdeZM5feI9t","html_url":"https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/1139","diff_url":"https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/1139.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/1139.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hazelgrove/hazel/issues/1139","number":1139,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"inexhaustive pattern examples in error messages","user":{"login":"karananand01","id":58492510,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NDkyNTEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58492510?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/karananand01","html_url":"https://github.com/karananand01","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karananand01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karananand01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karananand01/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karananand01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karananand01/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karananand01/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karananand01/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karananand01/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karananand01/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This pull request aims to produce a more verbose error displayed by the implementation of the exhaustiveness checking feature mentioned in “Live Pattern Matching with Typed Holes (https://victoryyw.github.io/assets/pdfs/pattern.pdf)”.\r\n\r\nIf a case expression is necessarily inexhaustive (i.e.: the expression will necessarily fail to match all values of the type of its scrutinee), the expression will be wrapped with an error hole like in Fig. 2b in the paper. This is done by using an error_exp called InexhaustiveMatch (created in #1114), which behaves uniquely when supplied to CursorInspector.re. We aim to supplement the produced error hole to display a pattern that can be produced by the case expression’s scrutinee but is not matched by any of the branches of the case expression.\r\n\r\nThis is planned to be done by utilizing the final constraint generated to produce the inexhaustive error and inverting it ( using the dual of the constraint ). The inverted constraint should include patterns that are not matched and therefore we can map the constraint to a pattern to be displayed on the error interface. \r\n","created_at":"2023-11-15T01:47:01Z","updated_at":"2026-04-21T13:00:30Z","closed_at":"2026-04-21T13:00:30Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[{"login":"DavidFangWJ","id":34878339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODc4MzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34878339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ","html_url":"https://github.com/DavidFangWJ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DavidFangWJ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"karananand01","id":58492510,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NDkyNTEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58492510?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/karananand01","html_url":"https://github.com/karananand01","followers_u